cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the version you used, together with the VISTA Data Descriptor."
title: "VISTA: processing code for the VIIRS-based global flood frequency record"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Andrea
    family-names: Amparore
  - given-names: Francesco
    family-names: Collivignarelli
  - given-names: Chloe
    family-names: Campo
  - given-names: Edoardo
    family-names: Forzano
  - given-names: Josef
    family-names: Clifford
repository-code: "https://github.com/un-fao/fao-vista"
url: "https://diem-vista.web.app/"
abstract: >-
  Processing code for VISTA, the VIIRS Surface Water Temporal Atlas: a global
  record of dekadal flood observations from 2012 to 2026, built from the
  NOAA/GMU VIIRS flood product at about 375 m resolution, with historical
  count, frequency and dominant-class products per dekad and per rolling
  month, computed in Google Earth Engine.
keywords:
  - flood mapping
  - surface water
  - VIIRS
  - remote sensing
  - Google Earth Engine
  - dekadal
  - FAO
license: MIT
